# Prisma-first backend planning (Schema + Mock)

When implementing new app features, keep a future backend Prisma schema up to date so backend work is easy later.

## Source of truth files

- **Prisma schema**: `prisma/schema.prisma`
- **Schema ↔ screen mapping**: `docs/backend/SCHEMA_MAP.md`
- **UI mock data**: `src/data/mockData.ts` (keep per project rule)
- **Backend seed plan (future)**: `mock/seed.ts` (mirrors Prisma models; no UI imports)

## Rules

- Every time UI introduces a new domain concept (Client, Appointment, Service, Product, Note, Payment, etc.), update `prisma/schema.prisma`.
- Keep stable IDs + timestamps on all models: `id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`.
- Store times as `DateTime` (UTC) in the database. Use ISO strings at the app boundary.
- Use join tables for many-to-many relationships (e.g. appointment services, used products).
- Prefer normalized relations + **snapshot fields** on join rows:
  - Example: `nameSnapshot`, `priceSnapshot` so historical visits don’t change when catalog updates.
- Keep UI types and backend schema aligned:
  - App types remain in `src/data/types.ts`
  - UI mocks remain in `src/data/mockData.ts`
  - Prisma schema lives in `prisma/` and is backend-focused

## Deliverables

- `prisma/schema.prisma` covers the whole app domain A→Z.
- `docs/backend/SCHEMA_MAP.md` documents screen/module → which tables/fields it needs.
- `mock/seed.ts` seeds a realistic dataset compatible with the Prisma schema (when backend starts).

